## **Advantages of Trees**  
✅ **Faster Searching** (BST reduces search time).  
✅ **Efficient Storage** (Trie for dictionaries).  
✅ **Better Organization** (Used in File Systems, Databases).  

## **Disadvantages of Trees**  
❌ **Complex to Implement** (Needs recursion and pointers).  
❌ **Uses More Memory** (Each node has pointers).  
❌ **Insertion/Deletion Can Be Costly** (In unbalanced trees).  

---

## **Tree vs Other Data Structures**  
| Feature | Tree | Linked List | Array |
|---------|------|------------|-------|
| **Searching** | Faster (O(log n) in BST) | Slow (O(n)) | Fast (O(1) in sorted) |
| **Memory Usage** | More (pointers used) | Less | Less |
| **Insertion/Deletion** | Moderate | Easy | Hard (shifting needed) |
| **Hierarchy** | Yes | No | No |

